{
 "encounter_id": "00868",
 "speakers": {
  "person_1": "PATIENT",
  "person_2": "DOCTOR",
  "person_3": "NURSE"
 },
 "turns": [
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "Mr Winters? I'm Alan, the nurse. Let me take your observations first. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Right. I don't mind. I itch, that's all. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "Blood pressure 152 over 88, pulse 74, temperature 36.6, oxygen 97 percent, weight 71 kilos.",
   "pause": 15.0
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Hello Mr Winters. It's the itching, isn't it? Tell me about it."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "All over. Mostly my back, my legs, my arms. Worse at night. I scratch until I bleed."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "How long has it been going on?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Two months. Since my kidneys got worse, I think."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Is there a rash?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No rash. Just the itch. My skin's dry."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any jaundice, or dark urine?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No. Nothing like that."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Remind me of your history."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Chronic kidney disease, for about eight years, and diabetes."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Do you smoke or drink?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Neither. Not for years."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any allergies?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Codeine. Makes me vomit."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Thank you. Let me look at your skin. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Go on.",
   "pause": 18.0
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "There's dry, scaly skin, and scratch marks on his back and arms, but no rash, and no signs of infection."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "Doctor, his last bloods came back this morning. Creatinine's up a bit, and phosphate is high. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Thank you, Alan. Mr Winters, the itch is very common in kidney disease, uraemic itch. I'd say that's what you've got, with dry skin adding to it."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Can it be treated? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Yes. First, moisturise twice a day with a plain thick cream, keep your showers short and lukewarm, and avoid scented soaps."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Right. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "I'd also like to start you on a tablet to lower your phosphate, calcium acetate, 500 mg, three times a day, with meals."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Will that help the itch? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Often, yes, because a high phosphate drives it. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "I'll go through the diet sheet with you, Mr Winters. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Thank you, Alan. I'd also like to arrange more blood tests, for your parathyroid hormone, calcium and liver tests, and a review with the kidney team."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Okay. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Keep your nails short, and wear cotton at night."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "I'll try. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "I'd like to see you again in four weeks."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Four weeks. Thank you. ~"
  }
 ],
